  "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{3}\u2061x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $81$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}\u2061x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{3}\u2061x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20613{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}\u20613(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}\u20613(2-1) \\\\  & =(4)\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
